{
 "design": "R6 what a battery with gaps costs, since few practitioners have all 125 cells.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 17:35 EDT). DataDecide ships every recipe at every size,\nwhich makes the design perfectly balanced and makes this paper's estimates easier to read than anything a\npractitioner will compute. Real comparisons drop cells, because a run crashed, because a size band was\nnever trained, or because a recipe was added late. Recipe clustering with unequal cluster sizes is the\ncase cluster-robust inference handles worst, and nothing in this paper says whether the interval survives\nit.\nThis run drops configurations at random and measures what happens. It removes a tenth, a quarter, a third\nand a half of the 125 cells, and it also removes a quarter in a lumpy way that takes whole recipes rather\nthan scattered cells, at 4,000 replicates each. Coverage that holds under scattered loss and falls under\nlumpy loss would tell a reader the interval cares about cluster balance rather than about sample size.\nSeed 20260974 keeps the draws distinct.\n",
